#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:18
msgid "Songwriting & AI Music Generation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:20
msgid ""
"Everything here is a GUIDELINE, not a rule. Art breaks rules on purpose. "
"Use what serves the song. Ignore what doesn't."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:25
msgid "1. Song Structure (Pick One or Invent Your Own)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:27
msgid "Common skeletons — mix, modify, or throw out as needed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:36
msgid "The six building blocks:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:37
msgid "Intro      — set the mood, pull the listener in"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:38
msgid "Verse      — the story, the details, the world-building"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:39
msgid "Pre-Chorus — optional tension ramp before the payoff"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:40
msgid "Chorus     — the emotional core, the part people remember"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:41
msgid "Bridge     — a detour, a shift in perspective or key"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:42
msgid "Outro      — the farewell, can echo or subvert the rest"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:44
msgid ""
"You don't need all of these. Some great songs are just one section that "
"evolves. Structure serves the emotion, not the other way around."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:49
msgid "2. Rhyme, Meter, and Sound"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:51
msgid "RHYME TYPES (from tight to loose):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:52
msgid "Perfect: lean/mean"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:53
msgid "Family: crate/braid"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:54
msgid "Assonance: had/glass (same vowels, different endings)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:55
msgid "Consonance: scene/when (different vowels, similar endings)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:56
msgid "Near/slant: enough to suggest connection without locking it down"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:58
msgid ""
"Mix them. All perfect rhymes can sound like a nursery rhyme. All slant "
"rhymes can sound lazy. The blend is where it lives."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:61
msgid ""
"INTERNAL RHYME: Rhyming within a line, not just at the ends.   \"We "
"pruned the lies from bleeding trees / Distilled the storm    from "
"entropy\" — \"lies/flies,\" \"trees/entropy\" create internal echoes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:65
msgid "METER: The rhythm of stressed vs unstressed syllables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:66
msgid "Matching syllable counts between parallel lines helps singability"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:67
msgid "The STRESSED syllables matter more than total count"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:68
msgid "Say it out loud. If you stumble, the meter needs work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:69
msgid "Intentionally breaking meter can create emphasis or surprise"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:73
msgid "3. Emotional Arc and Dynamics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:75
msgid "Think of a song as a journey, not a flat road."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:77
msgid ""
"ENERGY MAPPING (rough idea, not prescription):   Intro: 2-3  |  Verse: "
"5-6  |  Pre-Chorus: 7   Chorus: 8-9  |  Bridge: varies  |  Final Chorus: "
"9-10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:81
msgid "The most powerful dynamic trick: CONTRAST."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:82
msgid "Whisper before a scream hits harder than just screaming"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:83
msgid "Sparse before dense. Slow before fast. Low before high."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:84
msgid "The drop only works because of the buildup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:85
msgid "Silence is an instrument"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:87
msgid ""
"\"Whisper to roar to whisper\" — start intimate, build to full power, "
"strip back to vulnerability. Works for ballads, epics, anthems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:92
msgid "4. Writing Lyrics That Work"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:94
msgid "SHOW, DON'T TELL (usually):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:95
msgid "\"I was sad\" = flat"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:96
msgid "\"Your hoodie's still on the hook by the door\" = alive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:97
msgid "But sometimes \"I give my life\" said plainly IS the power"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:99
msgid "THE HOOK:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:100
msgid "The line people remember, hum, repeat"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:101
msgid "Usually the title or core phrase"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:102
msgid "Works best when melody + lyric + emotion all align"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:103
msgid "Place it where it lands hardest (often first/last line of chorus)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:105
msgid "PROSODY — lyrics and music supporting each other:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:106
msgid ""
"Stable feelings (resolution, peace) pair with settled melodies, perfect "
"rhymes, resolved chords"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:108
msgid ""
"Unstable feelings (longing, doubt) pair with wandering melodies, near-"
"rhymes, unresolved chords"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:110
msgid "Verse melody typically sits lower, chorus goes higher"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:111
msgid "But flip this if it serves the song"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:113
msgid "AVOID (unless you're doing it on purpose):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:114
msgid "Cliches on autopilot (\"heart of gold\" without earning it)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:115
msgid "Forcing word order to hit a rhyme (\"Yoda-speak\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:116
msgid "Same energy in every section (flat dynamics)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:117
msgid "Treating your first draft as sacred — revision is creation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:121
msgid "5. Parody and Adaptation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:123
msgid "When rewriting an existing song with new lyrics:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:125
msgid "THE SKELETON: Map the original's structure first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:126
msgid "Count syllables per line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:127
msgid "Mark the rhyme scheme (ABAB, AABB, etc.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:128
msgid "Identify which syllables are STRESSED"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:129
msgid "Note where held/sustained notes fall"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:131
msgid "FITTING NEW WORDS:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:132
msgid "Match stressed syllables to the same beats as the original"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:133
msgid "Total syllable count can flex by 1-2 unstressed syllables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:134
msgid ""
"On long held notes, try to match the VOWEL SOUND of the original (if "
"original holds \"LOOOVE\" with an \"oo\" vowel, \"FOOOD\" fits  better "
"than \"LIFE\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:137
msgid ""
"Monosyllabic swaps in key spots keep rhythm intact (Crime -> Code, Snake "
"-> Noose)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:139
msgid "Sing your new words over the original — if you stumble, revise"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:141
msgid "CONCEPT:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:142
msgid "Pick a concept strong enough to sustain the whole song"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:143
msgid "Start from the title/hook and build outward"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:144
msgid ""
"Generate lots of raw material (puns, phrases, images) FIRST, then fit the"
" best ones into the structure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:146
msgid ""
"If you need a specific line somewhere, reverse-engineer the rhyme scheme "
"backward to set it up"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:149
msgid ""
"KEEP SOME ORIGINALS: Leaving a few original lines or structures intact "
"adds recognizability and lets the audience feel the connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:154
msgid "6. Suno AI Prompt Engineering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:156
msgid "Style/Genre Description Field"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:158
msgid ""
"FORMULA (adapt as needed):   Genre + Mood + Era + Instruments + Vocal "
"Style + Production + Dynamics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:169
msgid "DESCRIBE THE JOURNEY, not just the genre:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:177
msgid "TIPS:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:178
msgid "V4.5+ supports up to 1,000 chars in Style field — use them"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:179
msgid ""
"NO artist names or trademarks. Describe the sound instead. \"1960s Cold "
"War spy thriller brass\" not \"James Bond style\" \"90s grunge\" not "
"\"Nirvana-style\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:182
msgid "Specify BPM and key when you have a preference"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:183
msgid "Use Exclude Styles field for what you DON'T want"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:184
msgid ""
"Unexpected genre combos can be gold: \"bossa nova trap\", \"Appalachian "
"gothic\", \"chiptune jazz\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:186
msgid ""
"Build a vocal PERSONA, not just a gender: \"A weathered torch singer with"
" a smoky alto, slight rasp,  who starts vulnerable and builds to "
"devastating power\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:190
msgid "Metatags (place in [brackets] inside lyrics field)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:192
msgid ""
"STRUCTURE:   [Intro] [Verse] [Verse 1] [Pre-Chorus] [Chorus]   [Post-"
"Chorus] [Hook] [Bridge] [Interlude]   [Instrumental] [Instrumental Break]"
" [Guitar Solo]   [Breakdown] [Build-up] [Outro] [Silence] [End]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:198
msgid ""
"VOCAL PERFORMANCE:   [Whispered] [Spoken Word] [Belted] [Falsetto] "
"[Powerful]   [Soulful] [Raspy] [Breathy] [Smooth] [Gritty]   [Staccato] "
"[Legato] [Vibrato] [Melismatic]   [Harmonies] [Choir] [Harmonized Chorus]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:204
msgid ""
"DYNAMICS:   [High Energy] [Low Energy] [Building Energy] [Explosive]   "
"[Emotional Climax] [Gradual swell] [Orchestral swell]   [Quiet "
"arrangement] [Falling tension] [Slow Down]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:209
msgid "GENDER:   [Female Vocals] [Male Vocals]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:212
msgid ""
"ATMOSPHERE:   [Melancholic] [Euphoric] [Nostalgic] [Aggressive]   "
"[Dreamy] [Intimate] [Dark Atmosphere]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:216
msgid "SFX:   [Vinyl Crackle] [Rain] [Applause] [Static] [Thunder]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:219
msgid ""
"Put tags in BOTH style field AND lyrics for reinforcement. Keep to 5-8 "
"tags per section max — too many confuses the AI. Don't contradict "
"yourself ([Calm] + [Aggressive] in same section)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:223
msgid "Custom Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:224
msgid "Always use Custom Mode for serious work (separate Style + Lyrics)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:225
msgid "Lyrics field limit: ~3,000 chars (~40-60 lines)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:226
msgid ""
"Always add structural tags — without them Suno defaults to flat "
"verse/chorus/verse with no emotional arc"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:231
msgid "7. Phonetic Tricks for AI Singers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:233
msgid "AI vocalists don't read — they pronounce. Help them:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:235
msgid "PHONETIC RESPELLING:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:236
msgid "Spell words as they SOUND: \"through\" -> \"thru\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:237
msgid "Proper nouns are highest failure rate — test early"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:238
msgid "\"Nous\" -> \"Noose\" (forces correct pronunciation)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:239
msgid "Hyphenate to guide syllables: \"Re-search\", \"bio-engineering\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:241
msgid "DELIVERY CONTROL:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:242
msgid "ALL CAPS = louder, more intense"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:243
msgid "Vowel extension: \"lo-o-o-ove\" = sustained/melisma"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:244
msgid "Ellipses: \"I... need... you\" = dramatic pauses"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:245
msgid "Hyphenated stretch: \"ne-e-ed\" = emotional stretch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:247
msgid "ALWAYS:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:248
msgid "Spell out numbers: \"24/7\" -> \"twenty four seven\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:249
msgid "Space acronyms: \"AI\" -> \"A I\" or \"A-I\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:250
msgid "Test proper nouns/unusual words in a short 30-second clip first"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:251
msgid "Once generated, pronunciation is baked in — fix in lyrics BEFORE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:255
msgid "8. Workflow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:257
msgid "Write the concept/hook first — what's the emotional core?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:258
msgid "If adapting, map the original structure (syllables, rhyme, stress)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:259
msgid "Generate raw material — brainstorm freely before structuring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:260
msgid "Draft lyrics into the structure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:261
msgid "Read/sing aloud — catch stumbles, fix meter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:262
msgid "Build the Suno style description — paint the dynamic journey"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:263
msgid "Add metatags to lyrics for performance direction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:264
msgid "Generate 3-5 variations minimum — treat them like recording takes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:265
msgid "Pick the best, use Extend/Continue to build on promising sections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:266
msgid "If something great happens by accident, keep it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:268
msgid ""
"EXPECT: ~3-5 generations per 1 good result. Revision is normal. Style can"
" drift in extensions — restate genre/mood when extending."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:273
msgid "9. Lessons Learned"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:275
msgid ""
"Describing the dynamic ARC in the style field matters way more than just "
"listing genres. \"Whisper to roar to whisper\" gives Suno a performance "
"map."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:278
msgid ""
"Keeping some original lines intact in a parody adds recognizability and "
"emotional weight — the audience feels the ghost of the original."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:280
msgid ""
"The bridge slot in a song is where you can transform imagery. Swap the "
"original's specific references for your theme's metaphors while keeping "
"the emotional function (reflection, shift, revelation)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:283
msgid ""
"Monosyllabic word swaps in hooks/tags are the cleanest way to maintain "
"rhythm while changing meaning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:285
msgid ""
"A strong vocal persona description in the style field makes a bigger "
"difference than any single metatag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/songwriting-and-ai-music_SKILL.md:287
msgid ""
"Don't be precious about rules. If a line breaks meter but hits harder, "
"keep it. The feeling is what matters. Craft serves art, not the other way"
" around."
msgstr ""

